# Frontend styling

Stack for all UI (Next.js apps, Electron renderer, `@repo/ui`):

- **Tailwind CSS** for layout and visuals
- **Radix primitives** (`@radix-ui/react-*`) for accessible behavior
- **shadcn/ui pattern** for components: Radix + Tailwind + `cn()` + `cva` variants + `className` forwarding

## Do

- Put Tailwind on the JSX: `className={cn("…", className)}`
- Shared primitives live in `@repo/ui`; keep app-local UI only when it is not reusable
- Variants via `cva` (class-variance-authority), not boolean-prop soup
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@repo/ui` or the app's `src/lib/cn.ts`

## Don't

- Do not add `styled-components` or new `*.styles.tsx`
- Do not use inline `style={{}}` except runtime values Tailwind cannot express (e.g. a session hex as a CSS variable)
- Do not wrap **new** components in `@radix-ui/themes` — use Radix primitives
- Do not introduce a second styling system in a file you are editing

## Legacy

Existing styled-components / Radix Themes code may stay until that file is touched. When you edit it, migrate that component to Tailwind + Radix primitives. Do not extend styled wrappers.
